{
  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_001: multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt+ViT-L, transformer, weighted → acc 0.520, F1 0.479), the most critical uncertainty is whether multimodal fusion is actually contributing meaningfully over a single strong modality. Config_008 (image_only, multiprofile, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool) uses the same image encoder (ViT-L) and profile setting (multiprofile) as config_001, cleanly isolating the image modality's contribution. If image-only accuracy is close to 0.52, it indicates the RNA branch is not adding value and remaining budget should focus on image-side optimization. If it is substantially lower, it confirms multimodal fusion is essential and we should invest in improving fusion/encoder choices. This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the fundamental architecture question before committing 8 remaining experiments to a specific direction."
}

